l,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n*Bugsquad edit*\nReproducible in master after 4.5 dev 3, likely due to #104269\nNot reproducible in: 4.5.dev3\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 Godot 4.5.dev3 Vulkan Forward+ Rendering\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm experiencing a severe FPS drop when physics interpolation is enabled and there are many static RigidBody3D or StaticBody3D nodes present in the scene, even if:\n\nThese bodies have no visual mesh attached,\n\nAll bodies are inactive/sleeping and not simulated,\n\nVisual debug shapes are disabled,\n\nThe rendering monitor shows no draw calls or primitives added when the FPS drops.\n\nWhen physics interpolation is turned off, the performance is normal.\nWhen it's on, the FPS can drop from over 1000 FPS down to ~70 FPS, even though nothing is visibly changing.\n\nNot related to debug shapes:\nThis issue is not caused by debug collision shapes. Debug rendering has been fully disabled in the project settings, and verified via the in-editor toggle.\nEven when the debug shape system is completely off, the performance drop persists as long as interpolation is enabled.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUse Godot 4.5.dev3 (latest as of this message).\n\nCreate a test scene with:\n\n~2000 RigidBody3D or StaticBody3D nodes with no visuals.\n\nphysics_interpolation_mode left enabled (default).\n\nRun with VSync disabled and monitor FPS.\n\nTry setting physics_interpolation_mode = Node.PHYSICS_INTERPOLATION_MODE_OFF manually on all bodies — it does not solve the issue.\n\nHowever, setting visible = false on the parent of those nodes (or removing them from the scene tree) does restore normal performance.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nMinimal Reproduction Project:\n📦 [ManyStaticColliders (1).zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20110265/ManyStaticColliders.1.zip)\n\nWhile running this project, FPS will hover between 50 and 100, despite there being no visuals.\nDisabling physics interpolation in project settings or toggling visibility on the nodes will cause FPS to jump back above 1000 FPS on most machines.\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106185/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106185/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}